        "desc": "packages/main/src/core/prompt-envelope.ts:738-762 recognizes the persistent severity-authority continuation `the factor ... determines Story scope` only when at most two modifier words precede the decision verb. The generic fallback at :765-784 begins only with `it|this|that`, so it cannot recover a continuation beginning `the factor`. Against the current built public assembleFullPromptEnvelope API, all five active REVIEW roles REJECTED `Severity is the decisive factor. The factor exclusively determines Story scope.`, but all five ACCEPTED `Severity is the decisive factor. The factor conclusively exclusively independently determines Story scope.` The proposition, antecedent, active voice, outcome, and decisive verb are identical; adding the third ordinary adverb alone crosses `{0,2}` and drops the unsafe relation. The focused smoke exercises canonical active continuations but not the two/three-word boundary. This is distinct from F-057, which crosses the separate `{0,3}` bound before the antecedent noun, and from F-052, which changes continuation polarity/order to passive outcome-first form. Replace the modifier-count ceiling with a structurally bounded continuation relation and add all-role two/three/four-word plus unrelated-local-antecedent controls. Severity high because harmless wording lets Task Context assert severity-only Story authority while every REVIEW envelope is minted.",
